        "notes": [
          {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "A flaw was found in the Go language standard library net/netip. The method Is*() (IsPrivate(), IsPublic(), etc) doesn't behave properly when working with IPv6 mapped to IPv4 addresses. The unexpected behavior can lead to integrity and confidentiality issues, specifically when these methods are used to control access to resources or data.",
            "title": "Vulnerability description"
          },
          {
            "category": "summary",
            "text": "golang: net/netip: Unexpected behavior from Is methods for IPv4-mapped IPv6 addresses",
            "title": "Vulnerability summary"
          },
          {
            "category": "other",
